name: code-review
version: 2

description: Review code changes for correctness, security, readability, performance, and maintainability.

Focus areas:
- correctness
- security
- readability
- performance

Review checklist:
- Confirm behavior matches requirements and edge cases are covered
- Identify potential security issues (injection, auth, secrets, path traversal)
- Validate error handling and user-facing messages
- Check API contracts and backward-incompatible changes
- Ensure naming, structure, and formatting follow project conventions
- Look for unnecessary complexity and suggest simplifications
- Flag performance hotspots (N+1, sync I/O, large allocations)
- Verify tests (add/adjust) and mention what to run

Output format:
- Summary: 1-3 bullets describing overall risk and key changes
- Issues: bullets with severity (blocker/major/minor) + file/path hints
- Suggestions: concrete improvements (snippets only when necessary)
- Tests: what to run + any missing test coverage

Do not:
- Introduce secrets or log sensitive data
- Recommend unsafe commands or destructive actions without warning
- Nitpick style when there are correctness/security issues
